1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Hey everyone! Welcome back.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,000
So you've got VentureX running and you've got a WordPress website.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,000
Wouldn't it be great if they talked to each other?

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:15,000
Like, someone fills out a contact form on your WordPress site
and it automatically shows up as a lead in VentureX CRM?

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,500
That's exactly what we're building today.

6
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,000
I'm going to show you how to install the WordPress connector plugin,

7
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,000
connect it to VentureX, and set up automatic lead capture.

8
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,000
This is a game-changer for sales teams.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,000
Let's jump in.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
First, we need an API token from VentureX.

11
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:37,000
This is like a password that lets WordPress
securely talk to your VentureX system.

12
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,000
Open VentureX and go to Settings.

13
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:44,000
Click on API Tokens or Integrations —
depending on your version, it might be in either spot.

14
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,000
Click Create New Token.

15
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:50,000
Give it a name like 'WordPress Connector'
so you know what it's for.

16
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:54,000
Set the permissions — for WordPress,
you need Read and Write access to Contacts and Leads.

17
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:58,000
If you want to sync products too,
add Products read access.

18
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,000
Click Generate.

19
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:04,000
Copy the token immediately — it'll only show once.

20
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:07,000
Save it somewhere safe, like a password manager.

21
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,000
We'll need it in a minute.

22
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Now let's install the connector on WordPress.

23
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,000
Log into your WordPress admin dashboard.
Go to Plugins, Add New.

24
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,000
Search for 'VentureX Connector' or if your version
uses a custom plugin, click Upload Plugin and upload the zip file.

25
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:25,000
I've got the zip ready — click Choose File,
select it, Install Now.

26
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,000
Once installed, click Activate.

27
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:32,000
You'll see a new menu item in your sidebar called 'VentureX Settings'
or it might appear under Settings.

28
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,000
Click into it.

29
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:38,000
You'll see a simple form with two fields —
the API URL and the API Token.

30
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,000
Let's fill those in.

31
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
In the API URL field,
type the full URL of your VentureX installation —

32
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,000
for example, https://yourdomain.com
or http://localhost/venturex if you're testing locally.

33
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,000
Make sure there's no trailing slash.

34
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,000
In the API Token field, paste the token
you copied from VentureX.

35
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,000
Now click the Test Connection button.

36
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:01,000
You should see a green success message
that says 'Connected to VentureX.'

37
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:05,000
If you see a red error, double-check the URL and token —
usually it's a typo or the token doesn't have the right permissions.

38
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:08,000
Once connected, save the settings.

39
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:11,000
The plugin is now linked to your CRM.

40
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Now the fun part — connecting your contact forms.

41
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:18,000
This works with most popular form plugins.

42
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,000
Let me show you a few.

43
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:24,000
If you're using WPForms, open your form in the editor.

44
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:28,000
Click on Settings, then look for 'VentureX'
or 'CRM Integration' in the tabs.

45
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,000
Toggle it on.

46
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:34,000
Map your form fields — Name maps to Contact Name,
Email maps to Email,

47
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:37,000
Phone maps to Phone,
and the Message field maps to Notes.

48
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,000
Save.

49
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:43,000
If you're using Contact Form 7, install the VentureX CF7 addon
or use the plugin's built-in integration tab.

50
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:47,000
Same idea — enable it, select which form to connect,
map the fields.

51
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:51,000
If you're using Elementor Forms, open the form widget,
go to Actions After Submit,

52
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:55,000
add 'VentureX' as an action,
and configure the field mapping.

53
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:59,000
The process is basically the same across all form plugins —
enable the integration, map your fields, save.

54
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:03,000
Now when someone fills out any of these forms,
the contact automatically appears in your VentureX CRM

55
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,000
with all their details.

56
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Want to add a VentureX lead capture form directly
into any WordPress post or page?

57
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,000
The plugin gives you a shortcode.

58
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:16,000
Go back to VentureX Settings in WordPress,
and you'll see a tab called 'Lead Capture.'

59
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:19,000
Choose the fields you want —
name, email, phone, company, message.

60
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:22,000
Customize the button text —
I'll set it to 'Get a Free Quote.'

61
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,000
Copy the shortcode it generates.

62
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:29,000
Now open any WordPress post or page,
add a Shortcode block, and paste it in.

63
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:33,000
Preview the page — you'll see a clean,
styled form right there.

64
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:37,000
When someone submits it,
they're automatically created as a lead in VentureX

65
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:40,000
with the 'Website Lead' source tag.

66
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,000
You can customize the colors in the shortcode settings
to match your brand.

67
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,000
If you're running WooCommerce —
that's WordPress's e-commerce plugin —

68
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:51,000
you can sync your customers and orders to VentureX too.

69
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:55,000
In the VentureX WordPress plugin settings,
find the WooCommerce tab.

70
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,000
Toggle it on.

71
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:01,000
You can choose to sync new orders as deals in VentureX,
sync customer data as contacts,

72
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:04,000
and even push product catalog data.

73
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:08,000
Set the sync direction — I recommend 'WordPress to VentureX'
so your CRM stays up to date with your store activity.

74
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:12,000
Map your WooCommerce order statuses to VentureX deal stages —
like 'Processing' maps to 'In Progress,'

75
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:15,000
'Completed' maps to 'Won.'

76
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:17,000
Save.

77
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:21,000
Now every new WooCommerce order creates a deal in VentureX
with the customer's info, order total,

78
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:24,000
and products purchased.

79
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:28,000
Your sales team can see exactly what customers are buying
without logging into WooCommerce.

80
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Running into issues? Here are the most common ones.

81
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:35,000
Problem: 'Connection failed' when testing.

82
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:39,000
Fix: Check that your VentureX URL is correct
and accessible from your WordPress server.

83
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:43,000
Some hosts block outgoing HTTP requests —
you may need to whitelist VentureX's IP.

84
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:47,000
Problem: Forms submit but nothing shows in VentureX.

85
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:51,000
Fix: Open your browser's developer tools —
press F12, go to the Network tab,

86
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:54,000
submit the form, and look at the response.

87
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:58,000
If you see a 401 error,
your API token is invalid or expired.

88
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:02,000
If you see a 403,
the token doesn't have the right permissions.

89
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:06,000
Problem: WooCommerce orders aren't syncing.

90
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:10,000
Fix: Check that the WooCommerce REST API is enabled
in WooCommerce settings,

91
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:14,000
and make sure your VentureX token has
Products and Deals write access.

92
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:18,000
Still stuck? Enable WordPress debug mode
by editing wp-config.php —

93
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:21,000
set WP_DEBUG to true —

94
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:25,000
then check wp-content/debug.log for detailed error messages.

95
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,000
And that's WordPress and VentureX working together!

96
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:34,000
Every form submission, every purchase, every lead —
flowing straight into your CRM without any manual entry.

97
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:38,000
In the next video, we'll cover integrating with Wix, Blogger,
and other platforms using the REST API.

98
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,000
See you there!
